# This directory ships as the public toft-install repository, and an
# operator can install straight into a clone of it: `./install.sh --dir .`.
# What that writes is .env — the only copy of ENCRYPTION_KEY, the JWT secret and
# the database password — into a git working tree whose remote is public. One
# `git add -A` later they are on GitHub, and rotating ENCRYPTION_KEY is not a
# thing that can be done to a database already encrypted with it.
#
# So the ignore travels with the bundle rather than living only in the
# repository this is authored in, where it protects nobody but us.
.env
install.log
backups/
